  abstract={This research analyses and compares the effectiveness of penetration testing tools to detect web application vulnerabilities. The penetration testing tools evaluated were Burp Suite Professional, Burp Suite Community, OWASP ZAP, Wfuzz, Hydra, and SQL Map. These tools have been tested in controlled environment. Regardless, Damn Vulnerable Web Application (DVWA), a real-world web application, which is equipped with different levels of security options, was used for this research. The key performance indicators that were analysed are the detection accuracy, ease of use, capability to integrate with another tool, and capability to generate a report. This research identifies security vulnerabilities that can be exploited and will help strengthen the organisation’s defence system. This proactive approach supports compliance, reduces risks and improves overall security posture.},
  keywords={Ethics;Accuracy;Source coding;Key performance indicator;Brute force attacks;Application security;Computer crime;Penetration testing;Testing;Web application security;Penetration testing tools;Vulnerability assessment;Brute force attack;Tool comparison;Ethical hacking;Cybersecurity},
